759 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Sprint Zero\n\nSprint Zero is an AI\055augmented product discovery framework for design leaders and product teams who can\047t afford to spend six weeks figuring out what to build\056 Traditional Design Sprints are powerful but slow\054 facilitation\055heavy\054 and hard to scale\056 Sprint Zero compresses a full discovery cycle into five structured days by orchestrating a small team of specialised AI agents \050research\054 ideation\054 critique\054 and validation\051 each handling a defined phase of the sprint\054 with the designer reviewing and steering at every gate\056\n\nThe approach is grounded in my 15\053 years of experience as a UX Designer\056 The project will be proven on a concrete case study\072 a UX teardown and redesign proposal for the Weather Underground app\054 evaluated through a European market lens\056\n\nData comes from app store reviews\054 competitor analysis\054 heuristic frameworks\054 and RITE sessions with real designers \050not synthetic AI proxies\051\056 The agents synthesise and challenge\073 the designer decides\056 AI is required because the volume of research synthesis\054 parallel ideation\054 and real\055time critique needed to run a credible 5\055day discovery cycle simply isn\047t achievable by a single practitioner working alone\056\n\nThe biggest blocker is the synthetic user trap\072 ensuring the validation agent generates hypotheses for real RITE sessions rather than simulating user responses\056 That distinction will be actively monitored and documented throughout\056 It\047s one of the things this project is specifically designed to test\056\n\nBy week 12\072 a working methodology\054 a documented case study\054 and a clear answer to the question nobody has properly answered yet\072 What does a designer actually do differently when agents join the process\077)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 760 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

760 0 obj
  << /K [ 759 0 R ]
     /P 967 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

761 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Project Description\n\n1\056 What problem are you solving\077 For whom\077\nTeams waste significant time and money building the wrong things\024or validating ideas too slowly\056\nProduct discovery today is often\072\nToo slow \050weeks or months\051\nToo subjective \050driven by opinions\054 not evidence\051\nPoorly connected to real user or market signals\nI\031m solving this for product teams\054 design leaders\054 and startups working in complex domains where decisions are costly and speed matters\056\n\n2\056 How is this currently solved\077 Why is your solution superior\077\nToday\054 teams rely on\072\nWorkshops like Design Sprints\nUser research cycles\nMarket analysis and stakeholder alignment sessions\nThese are valuable but\072\nResource\055heavy\nHard to scale\nOften disconnected from real\055time data\nMy approach\024an\240AI\055augmented Design Sprint\024compresses this into a structured\054 repeatable 5\055day framework where AI accelerates research\054 synthesis\054 ideation\054 and validation\056\nThe advantage\072\nFaster insights \050days vs weeks\051\nBroader exploration of ideas\nData\055informed\024not just opinion\055driven\024decisions\n\n3\056 Why does it matter\077 \050business impact\051\nReduces cost of building the wrong product\nSpeeds up time\055to\055market\nImproves quality of product decisions\nAligns teams faster around evidence\054 not opinions\nIn high\055stakes environments\054 this can mean\240millions saved or unlocked\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 762 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

762 0 obj
  << /K [ 761 0 R ]
     /P 967 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

763 0 obj
  << /ActualText (4\056 How does this map to your specialty\077\nThis builds directly on my experience designing complex\054 high\055risk systems in finance\054 compliance\054 and investment platforms\056\nIn these environments\072\nDecisions are expensive\nDiscovery is slow and fragmented\nTeams struggle to align\nThis project extends my work into\240AI\055powered decision support for product strategy\054 not just product design\056\n\n5\056 Where is the data coming from\077\nThe system will leverage\072\nInternal product data \050where available\051\nUser research inputs \050interviews\054 feedback\054 usability data\051\nMarket and competitor data\nSynthetic data generated by AI to explore edge cases and scenarios\n\n6\056 Why does this require AI\077\nWithout AI\054 this process remains manual\054 slow\054 and limited in scope\056\nAI enables\072\nRapid synthesis of large amounts of research\nPattern detection across fragmented data\nGeneration of multiple solution directions\nSimulation of user behaviors and edge cases\nIt fundamentally\240changes the speed and scale of discovery\056\n\n7\056 What will AI agents do\077\nAI agents will act as specialized collaborators across the sprint\072\nResearch agent \222 synthesizes insights from multiple sources\nIdeation agent \222 generates and expands solution directions\nCritique agent \222 challenges assumptions and identifies risks\nValidation agent \222 simulates user reactions and tests concepts\nThe goal is not to replace humans\054 but to\240augment decision\055making and reduce blind spots\056\n\n8\056 Biggest risks \057 blockers\nRisk of over\055reliance on AI\055generated insights vs real user data\nTrust\072 teams may question the validity of AI\055supported outputs\nIntegration into existing workflows \050change resistance\051\nEnsuring outputs are actionable\024not just interesting)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 764 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

