765 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Starting with the system \050not the agents\051\nSprintZero\240should behave like a pipeline\072\nINPUT \222 DISCOVERY \222 SYNTHESIS \222 IDEATION \222 VALIDATION \222 OUTPUT\nEach stage \075\240one responsibility\050Each responsibility \075\240one agent \050or tightly scoped pair\051\nI If you don\031t enforce this\054 agents become noisy generalists\056\n\n\231\017 Recommended Agent Architecture\n\257 Orchestrator \050the brain\051\nControls flow across stages\nDecides which agent to call\nMaintains context of the sprint\nIn OpenClaw terms\072\nThis is your main workflow \057 entry agent\nShould NOT do heavy thinking\024just routing \053 memory\n\n\015 1\056 Research Agent\nGoal\072\240Gather and structure raw inputs\nResponsibilities\072\nMarket scan\nCompetitor analysis\nUser input summarization\nTrend extraction\nSkills \057 plugins to use\072\nEnable\072\240google\054 \050optionally enable\240tavily\240or\240duckduckgo\051\nConsider enabling\072\240firecrawl\240\050currently disabled \222 you should enable it\051\nI Right now you\031re missing a\240proper web ingestion layer\056 Fix that\056\n\n\351 2\056 Synthesis Agent\nGoal\072\240Turn chaos into insights\nResponsibilities\072\nCluster patterns\nExtract jobs\055to\055be\055done\nIdentify pain points\nPrioritize opportunities\nSkills\072\nPure LLM reasoning \050OpenAI \057 Anthropic \057 Mistral\051\nI This is where your UX strength should shine\056\050Don\031t let it become \034summarize this\056\035\n\n\241 3\056 Ideation Agent\nGoal\072\240Generate solution directions\nResponsibilities\072\nGenerate multiple concepts\nExplore variations\nExpand ideas beyond obvious solutions\nSkills\072\nLLM \053 possibly synthetic provider \050you already have it enabled\051\nI Important\072 constrain it with inputs from synthesis or it becomes fluff generator\056\n\n\226\017 4\056 Critique Agent \050underrated but critical\051\nGoal\072\240Challenge ideas\nResponsibilities\072\nIdentify risks\nDetect assumptions\nHighlight edge cases\nStress\055test ideas\nI This is where most AI systems fail\024they only generate\054 never critique\056\n\n\352 5\056 Validation Agent\nGoal\072\240Simulate reality\nResponsibilities\072\nSimulate user reactions\nEvaluate feasibility\nScore ideas \050confidence\054 risk\054 impact\051\nSkills\072\nSynthetic \053 reasoning models\nI This is your differentiator if done right\056\n\n\376 6\056 Output Agent\nGoal\072\240Produce structured deliverables\nResponsibilities\072\nSprint summary\nKey decisions\nRecommendations\nNext steps\n\n\004 Orchestration Flow \050this is the core\051\nIn OpenClaw\054 define something like\072\norchestrator\072\050  step\1371 \222 research\137agent\050  step\1372 \222 synthesis\137agent\050  step\1373 \222 ideation\137agent\050  step\1374 \222 critique\137agent\050  step\1375 \222 validation\137agent\050  step\1376 \222 output\137agent\nI Critical\072\nPass structured outputs between agents \050JSON if possible\051\nAvoid passing raw text blobs\n\n\361 Memory Strategy \050you\031re underusing this\051\nYou already have at the current OpenClaw setup\072\nmemory\055core\240enabled \005\nBut that\031s not enough\056\nYou should define\072\nSprint memory \050short\055term\051\240\222 current run\nKnowledge memory \050long\055term\051\240\222 reusable insights\nI Consider enabling\072\nmemory\055lancedb\240\050currently disabled\051\nThis allows\072\nRetrieval across multiple sprints\nBuilding a\240compounding discovery system\n\n\352 Example Task Flow \050concrete\051\nInput\072\n\034Explore opportunity in fraud detection UX for retail users\035\nFlow\072\nResearch Agent\050\222 pulls fraud trends\054 competitors\054 common scams\nSynthesis Agent\050\222 identifies key problems \050e\056g\056 trust gap\054 false positives\051\nIdeation Agent\050\222 generates solutions \050browser tool\054 scoring system\054 alerts\051\nCritique Agent\050\222 flags risks \050false trust\054 liability\054 regulation\051\nValidation Agent\050\222 simulates user reactions \053 scores concepts\nOutput Agent\050\222 produces structured sprint report)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 766 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
