771 0 obj
  << /ActualText (My current thinking is to keep a very strict boundary\072 the validation agent won\031t simulate users or generate \034answers\054\035 but instead will synthesise hypotheses\054 tensions\054 and test scenarios based on the prior agents\031 outputs\056 So essentially\072 it prepares the\240questions\054 not the\240evidence\056\n\nFor actual validation\054 I plan to run lightweight RITE sessions with real designers \050likely peers\051\054 capture transcripts\054 and then feed those back into the system as structured input for the next iteration\056 Over time\054 I want to see if the agent can meaningfully improve the quality of what we choose to test\056 Not replace the testing itself\056\n\nI\031m deliberately treating this as a constraint rather than a limitation\054 because the synthetic user shortcut feels like the fastest way to lose credibility\056)
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 772 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

