775 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This storyboard explores a narrow slice of my broader project\054\240Sprint Zero\072 the moment where a designer needs to extract a meaningful insight from messy\054 unstructured research under time pressure\056\n\nThe scenario focuses on a common situation\024reviewing large volumes of qualitative data \050app store reviews\054 research notes\051 and struggling to move from raw input to a clear\054 defensible point of view\056\n\nThe AI system is intentionally represented in a simple way\056 At this stage\054 the goal is not to define an agentic architecture\054 but to test whether a believable interaction can produce a better outcome than current workflows\056\n\nThe key shift illustrated in the storyboard is not automation\054 but\240the introduction of structured synthesis and critique\056 Instead of generating answers\054 the system\072\norganises signals into patterns\nsurfaces contradictions and gaps\nchallenges the designer\031s assumptions\nThe designer remains fully in control of the final decision\056\n\nThe payoff is deliberately modest\072 a single\054 more precise and testable insight\056 The objective is to demonstrate improved\240quality of thinking\054 not speed or completeness\056\n\nNote\072\240I initially considered developing a \034before\057after\035 comparison storyboard to contrast this flow with current practices \050including ad\055hoc use of tools like ChatGPT\051\056 Due to time constraints\054 I focused on the \034after\035 scenario\056 However\054 exploring that contrast further is something I plan to revisit\054 particularly to better understand the variability in how designers currently incorporate AI into their workflows\056\n\nQuestion for the group\072\nI realised while doing this that I don\031t have a clear picture of what the \034before\035 actually looks like across different teams\056\n\nWhen you\031re working with messy research inputs \050e\056g\056 reviews\054 notes\054 transcripts\051\054 how do you typically get to a point where you feel confident enough to call something an \034insight\035\077\nWhat does your process actually look like \050not ideal\054 but real\051\077\nWhere do you tend to get stuck or second\055guess yourself\077\nAre you using any AI tools in that step today\077 If yes\054 where do they help\054 and where do they fall short\077)
     /K [ 13 ]
     /P 776 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

