875 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This digital twin represents the minimum set of inputs\054 transformations\054 and outputs required to support the interaction shown in the storyboard\056\nIt is intentionally kept at the level of\240functional capabilities rather than technical implementation\054 focusing on what the system must do to make the outcome believable\056\n\n\nINPUTS\nThe system draws from multiple sources of qualitative and contextual data\072\nApp store reviews \050text\051\nResearch outputs \050notes\054 interview transcripts\051\nCompetitor screenshots \050images\051\nHeuristic frameworks and design principles\nDesigner input \050context\054 goals\054 prompts\051\nThese inputs reflect the fragmented nature of real\055world discovery work\056\n\nSCHEMATIC \050Core Capabilities\051\nThe system processes inputs through a series of high\055level capabilities\072\nText understanding\050Clustering themes\054 identifying patterns\054 and detecting sentiment in qualitative data\nVisual understanding\050Extracting UI patterns and feature signals from competitor screenshots\nSynthesis\050Aligning signals across sources to identify overlaps\054 gaps\054 and emerging themes\nCritique\050Surfacing contradictions\054 highlighting potential biases\054 and exposing weak assumptions\nInsight framing\050Structuring outputs into clear\054 testable insights that the designer can refine\nThese components are represented abstractly and will later evolve into a more explicit agentic structure\056\n\nOUTPUTS\nThe system produces structured\054 inspectable outputs to support decision\055making\072\nThematic clusters with supporting evidence\nContradictions and tensions across data sources\nIdentified blind spots or missing perspectives\nConfidence signals and potential biases\nFramed insight proposals \050editable and owned by the designer\051\nThe system does not produce final answers\054 but rather\240improves the quality and reliability of the thinking process\056)
     /K [ 63 ]
     /P 876 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

