879 0 obj
  << /ActualText (\072\nWhat about building it for quantitative research first\077 I\031d say having it build AI to provide\240trustworthy\240insights into qualitative research is way too complex\054 because qualitative research is more about humans and psychology\056 Or maybe have a thin slice \055 what part of research \050maybe transcripts\057notes\054 rather than interviews\051 should AI summarize\077\050I wouldn\031t give AI to summarize video interviews\054 or at least I\031d hardly trust it\054 at this point\056\n\050My responce\072\nThanks Milena\054\050This is a really thoughtful challenge\054 and I think you\031re pointing at something important\056\nI agree that jumping straight into \034AI generating trustworthy qualitative insights\035 is a big leap\054 especially given how much of qualitative work relies on nuance\054 context\054 and interpretation\056 If anything\054 that\031s exactly the part I\240don\031t\240want the system to pretend it can fully replace\056\nYour suggestion to thin\055slice further \050e\056g\056 focusing on transcripts\057notes rather than interviews themselves\051 resonates\056 It\031s closer to where I\031m currently leaning\072 treating AI as a way to structure and stress\055test signals that already exist\054 rather than interpret raw human behaviour end\055to\055end\056\nOn the quantitative angle\054 it\031s an interesting trade\055off\056 It would definitely be easier to model and validate\054 but I\031m consciously starting with qualitative because that\031s where I see the biggest friction today \050and also the highest risk of \034plausible but wrong\035 outputs\054 which I want to confront head\055on\051\056\nCompletely with you on video interviews\054 by the way\056 At this stage\054 I\031d be very cautious trusting any system to meaningfully interpret them beyond surface\055level summaries\056\nYour comment actually helped me realise that the real boundary I need to define is not\240what AI can process\054 but\240what it should be trusted to conclude\056 That\031s something I\031ll try to make much clearer in the next iteration\056)
     /K [ 66 ]
     /P 880 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

