919 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Assumptions \046 Reflections\n\nComing back to this assignment a couple of weeks later\054 I found the Value Matrix particularly useful in forcing a shift from \034interesting idea\035 to\240economic reality\056\nMy initial instinct with Sprint Zero was to frame value in terms of speed and efficiency \050faster discovery\054 compressed timelines\051\056 However\054 this exercise pushed me to identify the\240core prediction that actually creates value\056\n\nAI Question\nI narrowed the scope down to a single decision point\072\n\034Is this emerging theme significant enough to investigate as a real product insight\077\035\nThis reflects the moment in the storyboard where the designer moves from raw signals to something worth acting on\056\n\nKey Assumptions\nTo make the matrix concrete\054 I made a number of simplifying assumptions\072\nThe system is used by a small product team \050Designer \053 PM\051 in a typical discovery cycle\nAround \17620 potential \034themes\035 are evaluated per cycle\nTime is the primary cost driver \050using rough \2540\0565\023\2541\057min heuristics from the course\051\nThe impact of decisions is approximated through\072\ntime spent investigating\nopportunity cost of missed insights\ndownstream product impact\nThe numbers are intentionally rough\054 but directionally grounded\056\n\nWhat Became Clear\n1\056\240This is a prioritisation problem\054 not a generation problem\nThe value is not in producing insights\054 but in helping teams decide\072\nwhat is worth attention\nwhat is noise\nThis reframed Sprint Zero from an \034insight generator\035 into a\240decision\055support system\056\n\n2\056\240False Negatives are disproportionately expensive\nMissing a valuable signal \050FN\051 has a much higher cost than investigating a weak one \050FP\051\056\nThis has an important implication\072\nThe system should likely optimise for\240recall over precision\050\050i\056e\056 surface more potential opportunities\054 even with some noise\051\nThis runs counter to the instinct to \034cleanly filter\035 outputs\056)
     /K [ 86 ]
     /P 920 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

920 0 obj
  << /K [ 919 0 R ]
     /P 967 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

921 0 obj
  << /ActualText (3\056\240Trust is tied to transparency\054 not accuracy\nGiven the ambiguity of \034insight quality\054\035 the system cannot rely on being \034correct\056\035\nInstead\054 value comes from\072\nexposing reasoning\nsurfacing contradictions\nmaking uncertainty visible\nThis directly connects back to the critique layer explored in the storyboard and digital twin\056\n\nLimitations \057 Open Questions\nThe financial values \050especially for False Negatives\051 are based on proxy assumptions and would need validation in a real product context\nThe definition of a \034valuable insight\035 remains subjective and context\055dependent\nThe model assumes a relatively linear discovery process\054 which may not reflect all team dynamics\n\nReflection\nThis exercise highlighted how ambitious the broader Sprint Zero concept is\056\nReducing it to a single prediction forced clarity on\072\nwhere value is actually created\nwhat kind of errors matter most\nand how the system should behave under uncertainty\nIf anything\054 it reinforced that the success of this concept will depend less on generating outputs\054 and more on\240how well it supports judgment under ambiguity\056)
     /K [ 87 ]
     /P 922 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

