935 0 obj
  << /ActualText (RAG File \050First Draft with ChatGPT\051\n\nRAG File\072 Insight Evaluation \024 Weather App \050EU Context\051\n1\056 Context\nThis dataset represents a small sample of qualitative inputs related to a weather application used in Europe\056 The goal is to evaluate whether emerging themes are significant enough to investigate as product insights\056\n\n2\056 Raw Signals \050User Reviews\051\n\034Forecast says sunny and then it rains 10 minutes later\056 Happens all the time in spring\056\035\n\034Weather accuracy is unreliable during seasonal changes\056\035\n\034It\031s not that it\031s always wrong\054 but I don\031t trust it anymore\056\035\n\034Too many ads\054 but I could live with that if forecasts were more consistent\056\035\n\034Rain predictions are especially bad where I live \050Zurich area\051\056\035\n\034Sometimes it\031s accurate\054 sometimes completely off\056 Hard to rely on\056\035\n\034The UI is fine\054 but I check another app to confirm the forecast\056\035\n\034Feels like it doesn\031t handle local microclimates well\056\035\n\n3\056 Research Notes \050Synthesised Observations\051\nUsers do not necessarily expect perfect accuracy\nTrust is impacted more by\240inconsistency\240than by occasional errors\nSeasonal transitions \050spring\057autumn\051 increase perceived unreliability\nUsers cross\055check with other apps \222 signal of low confidence\nComplaints about UI are secondary to trust issues\n\n4\056 Heuristic Framework \050Evaluation Rules\051\nA theme is more likely to be significant if\072\nIt appears across multiple independent sources\nIt reflects behaviour change \050e\056g\056 switching apps\054 double\055checking\051\nIt highlights loss of trust rather than isolated frustration\nIt is context\055specific \050e\056g\056 geography\054 seasonality\051\nIt connects to product decisions \050not just general complaints\051\nA theme is less reliable if\072\nIt is generic \050e\056g\056 \034UI is confusing\035\051\nIt lacks behavioural evidence\nIt is driven by a vocal minority\nIt cannot be linked to a concrete product implication\n\n5\056 Example Themes to Evaluate\nTheme A\072\n\034Users complain about weather accuracy\035\nTheme B\072\n\034Users lose trust during seasonal transitions due to inconsistent forecasts\054 leading them to verify forecasts with other apps\035\n\n6\056 Task for the Model\nFor each theme\072\nAssess whether it is significant enough to investigate\nIdentify supporting and contradicting evidence\nHighlight potential biases or gaps\nSuggest a refined\054 testable insight\n\n7\056 Example of a Strong Insight \050Reference\051\n\034European users lose trust in weather forecasts during seasonal transitions\024not because forecasts are always wrong\054 but because uncertainty is not communicated\054 leading to verification behaviour across multiple apps\056\035\n\n8\056 Example of a Weak Insight \050Reference\051\n\034Users want more accurate weather forecasts\056\035)
     /K [ 94 ]
     /P 936 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

