937 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Create the first draft of the RAG file for me\056\050\nCourse Assignment\072 Create your RAG\nReview your Storyboard\054 Digital Twin\054 and Value Matrix\056 Think about your system \024 what is the most important aspect\077  \034The thing without which nothing else would work\077\035 Now that you have that\054 build a simple RAG file to help the LLM generate the response for a thin slice of your data\056 Try to find the narrowest \034thinnest slice\035 of your use case that delivers value to the customer\056 \050Don\031t worry about making it Agentic yet\054 just use a simple AI representation as we discussed in class \024 we will revisit your RAG a few more times and make your data retrieval Agentic explicitly later in the course\056\051\nSuccess tips\072\nUse the use case from your Value Matrix\nFind some real data if possible \050use Google or your LLM\051\nThin\055slice the data to the smallest slice\nIterate until your LLM outputs something in the neighborhood of what you expected\nOptionally judge it \050see video\051\nYou can create either\072\nOne or more individual RAG files or\nRAG registry or\nIndividual RAG files \053 RAG Registry that work together\n \024 your choice\054 depending on the complexity of your use case and your comfort with AI data management systems\056\050\nI don\047t have examples or real data to use\054 but I can I can copy\055paste the appstore reviews from this link for you\072 )
     /K [ 95 ]
     /P 940 0 R
     /Pg 749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

